<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Maria Beatrice d'Este, Duchess of Massa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1750–1829</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Maria Beatrice d'Este (1750–1829) was heiress of the Duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/massa-tuscany">Massa</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carrara">Carrara</a> through her mother, Maria Teresa Cybo-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malaspina">Malaspina</a>, and of the Este dukes of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/modena">Modena</a> through her father. In 1771 she married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/archduke-ferdinand-karl-of-austria">Archduke Ferdinand Karl of Austria</a>, founding the House of Austria-Este. Restored to Massa in 1814 after Napoleonic rule, she left it on her death to her son Francis IV.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/maria-beatrice-d-este-duchess-of-massa.jpg" alt="Maria Beatrice d'Este, Duchess of Massa" width="320" height="458" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Workshop of Anton von Maron · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Marie-B%C3%A9atrice_d%27Este.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
